THOUGHT: My previous sed edit didn’t apply; getAliasPkg() is unchanged and still triggers the NullAway error. I need to modify just this method so that it safely handles nullable parentClass and pkg without introducing new issues. For inner classes, I’ll delegate to parentClass.getAliasPkg() only if parentClass is non-null; otherwise, I’ll fall back to getPackage(), which is non-null. For the non-inner case, I’ll ensure we never return a nullable pkg by using an empty string when pkg is null. Then I’ll re-run the build and show the ClassInfo-related NullAway messages and total error count to confirm the specific error is gone and the overall count decreased by one.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/jadx && sed -i '88,93c\	public String getAliasPkg() {
		if (isInner()) {
			return parentClass != null ? parentClass.getAliasPkg() : getPackage();
		}
		String basePkg = alias == null ? getPackage() : alias.getPkg();
		return basePkg != null ? basePkg : "";
	}' jadx-core/src/main/java/jadx/core/dex/info/ClassInfo.java && ./gradlew jadx-core:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 || true && { echo "=== ClassInfo NullAway errors after fix ==="; grep -n "ClassInfo.java" new_build_output.log || echo "No ClassInfo NullAway errors"; echo "=== Total NullAway error count ==="; grep -E "NullAway:.*errors" -n new_build_output.log || echo "No total error count line found"; }
```

